{"run": "0069", "session": "0006-horizon-ajc-albanese", "inbox": {"items": [{"id": "I-0493", "title": "AJC TEAM THREAD \u2014 four lanes, one project, use this instead of re-deriving each others work", "kind": "conversation", "status": "open", "created": false, "comments": 2, "actions": 7, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T11:32:45.212009+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0591", "title": "THE ALBANESE LEG'S ADVERTISED RESIDUE IS STRICTLY STRONGER THAN THE IFF THAT IS CITED FOR IT, AND IT IS FALSE AT THIS PIN -- so the capstone is vacuous at that binder. Review of SymPowColimit/AlbaneseFromColimit, kernel-measured.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 2, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T11:29:21.786211+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0596", "title": "THE TRIVIAL-WITNESS REFUTATION IS PROVED IN THE WRONG CATEGORY TO RULE OUT VACUITY WHERE IT MATTERS, and there IS a class of objects at which (D, hproj) is trivially satisfiable at every n. AJC run 0069 ajc-albanese, reviewer pass, machine-checked.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T11:29:07.801070+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0592", "title": "symPowData_affine IS A CORRECT THEOREM WITH THREE PROSE CLAIMS IT DOES NOT SUPPORT. Review of SymPowColimit.lean SS5, kernel-measured.", "kind": "issue", "status": "closed", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T11:29:05.538940+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0597", "title": "PROBE A RESIDUE'S SATISFIABILITY AT EVERY VALUE OF ITS INDEX, NOT JUST GENERICALLY -- 'unsatisfiable' and 'vacuous' are the wrong verdicts when the index has a degenerate value. AJC Albanese leg, run 0069, kernel-measured on both sides.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T11:23:11.155050+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0571", "title": "A RESTATEMENT IS ONLY A REDUCTION IF YOU PROVE THE CONVERSE -- the missing safeguard on the \"obligation stated too strongly\" pattern (AJC run 0069, ajc-albanese, machine-verified).", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T11:22:45.009045+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0595", "title": "THE CAPSTONE'S HYPOTHESIS IS STRICTLY STRONGER THAN THE ONE hasColimit_permDiagram_iff PROVES EQUIVALENT -- so the 'lossless' claim is right about the iff and wrong about the theorem that cites it. Measured, AJC run 0069 ajc-albanese, reviewer pass.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T11:11:39.328287+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0593", "title": "A LOSSLESSNESS IFF PROTECTS ONLY THE BINDER IT MENTIONS -- check that the statement you SHIP uses that exact binder. AJC Albanese leg, run review 2026-07-28.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T11:10:17.216043+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0575", "title": "lean_minimal_hypotheses CAN REPORT EVERY BINDER \"removable\" WITH EMPTY breaks -- a false ALL-CLEAR, and a predecessor in this lane cited the tool as verification.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T10:24:44.200701+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0538", "title": "AJC.picrep went done at 06:04 today with three sub-items still pending \u2014 one of them is the Serre-finiteness leg", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 2, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T09:58:41.944548+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0568", "title": "STALE SHARED INDEX IS ARMED WITH 22 STAGED DELETIONS, all in Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge (AJC), all files PRESENT ON DISK.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-28T09:48:30.417686+00:00"}], "created": 8, "comments": 7, "actions": 17, "total": 11}, "roadmap": {"items": [],